WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.400
The story of the bear shark.

00:04.500 --> 00:08.100
I was working at Airbnb,

00:08.300 --> 00:10.500
and I had gained a reputation for myself

00:10.550 --> 00:13.700
as the guy you call when you need something done.

00:14.700 --> 00:17.500
And lo and behold,

00:17.550 --> 00:22.100
my friend Brendan had been authorized by the company

00:22.150 --> 00:26.900
to build a life-size, 12-foot bear shark.

00:27.800 --> 00:29.900
Bear in the front, shark in the back,

00:29.950 --> 00:33.000
to be hung above the staircase.

00:33.900 --> 00:37.950
And when he ordered the two giant foam blocks

00:38.000 --> 00:42.600
to assemble the sculpture,

00:42.900 --> 00:47.400
they arrived…

00:47.600 --> 00:51.250
as giant blocks in his apartment lobby,

00:51.300 --> 00:57.600
too large to get into the room.

00:58.200 --> 01:01.000
And so…

01:08.300 --> 01:10.400
…he called me up.

01:11.600 --> 01:15.900
My solution was to borrow one of his guitar strings

01:17.700 --> 01:22.900
and hook it up into my car battery

01:23.400 --> 01:27.700
and make a makeshift hot wire

01:28.050 --> 01:30.100
to slice through the foam

01:30.150 --> 01:33.800
and get it into the studio.
